<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>

<LinearLayout
    xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent"
    android:orientation="vertical"
    android:gravity="center"
    android:padding="16dp">

    <TextView
        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:text="Hello Widget!"
        android:textSize="20sp"
        android:textStyle="bold" />

    <Button
    android:id="@+id/widget_button"
    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
    android:layout_marginTop="12dp"
    android:text="Open App" />

</LinearLayout>


<!--    Yes. First, there is **one typo** in your XML:-->

<!--    `<LinerLayout>` ❌ should be `<LinearLayout>` ✅-->

<!--    Now let's understand it **line by line**.-->

<!--    ### 1. XML declaration-->

<!--    ```xml-->
<!--    <?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    * `<?xml ... ?>` → tells Android that this file is an **XML document**.-->
<!--    * `version="1.0"` → XML version being used.-->
<!--    * `encoding="utf-8"` → tells XML to use UTF-8 character encoding.-->
<!--    * `?>` → ends the XML declaration.-->

<!--    This is basically metadata about the XML file.-->

<!--    -&#45;&#45;-->

<!--    ### 2. Root layout-->

<!--    ```xml-->
<!--    <LinearLayout-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    `LinearLayout` is a **container**.-->

<!--    Think of it as a box that can contain other UI elements:-->

<!--    ```text-->
<!--    LinearLayout-->
<!--    │-->
<!--    ├── TextView-->
<!--    │-->
<!--    └── Button-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    The important thing is that `LinearLayout` arranges its children **in a line**.-->

<!--    You specify whether that line is:-->

<!--    * `vertical` → top to bottom-->
<!--    * `horizontal` → left to right-->

<!--    Your code uses vertical.-->

<!--    ⚠️ Your original says `LinerLayout`, which is invalid. It must be:-->

<!--    ```xml-->
<!--    <LinearLayout-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    -&#45;&#45;-->

<!--    ### 3. Android XML namespace-->

<!--    ```xml-->
<!--    xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    This is very important.-->

<!--    `xmlns:android` defines the **Android XML namespace**.-->

<!--    Because of this, Android understands attributes such as:-->

<!--    ```xml-->
<!--    android:layout_width-->
<!--    android:layout_height-->
<!--    android:text-->
<!--    android:gravity-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    You can think of it as saying:-->

<!--    > "The attributes starting with `android:` belong to Android."-->

<!--    The URL doesn't mean your app is making an internet request. It's simply the namespace identifier.-->

<!--    -&#45;&#45;-->

<!--    ### 4. Width of the LinearLayout-->

<!--    ```xml-->
<!--    android:layout_width="match_parent"-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    `layout_width` → controls the width.-->

<!--    `match_parent` → make the LinearLayout as wide as its parent allows.-->

<!--    So if the screen is:-->

<!--    ```text-->
<!--    ┌─────────────────────────┐-->
<!--    │                         │-->
<!--    │                         │-->
<!--    │                         │-->
<!--    └─────────────────────────┘-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    The LinearLayout takes the entire available width.-->

<!--    -&#45;&#45;-->

<!--    ### 5. Height of the LinearLayout-->

<!--    ```xml-->
<!--    android:layout_height="match_parent"-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    Same idea, but for height.-->

<!--    `match_parent` → take all available height.-->

<!--    So your root layout becomes essentially the **whole widget layout area**.-->

<!--    -&#45;&#45;-->

<!--    ### 6. Orientation-->

<!--    ```xml-->
<!--    android:orientation="vertical"-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    This tells `LinearLayout` how to arrange its children.-->

<!--    `vertical` means:-->

<!--    ```text-->
<!--    TextView-->
<!--    ↓-->
<!--    Button-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    If you used:-->

<!--    ```xml-->
<!--    android:orientation="horizontal"-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    you would get:-->

<!--    ```text-->
<!--    TextView   Button-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    So in your widget:-->

<!--    ```text-->
<!--    ┌─────────────────────┐-->
<!--    │                     │-->
<!--    │    Hello Widget!    │-->
<!--    │                     │-->
<!--    │     [Open App]      │-->
<!--    │                     │-->
<!--    └─────────────────────┘-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    -&#45;&#45;-->

<!--    ### 7. Gravity-->

<!--    ```xml-->
<!--    android:gravity="center"-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    This controls how the **children inside the LinearLayout** are positioned.-->

<!--    `center` means center them.-->

<!--    So instead of:-->

<!--    ```text-->
<!--    ┌─────────────────────┐-->
<!--    │ Hello Widget!       │-->
<!--    │ [Open App]          │-->
<!--    │                     │-->
<!--    └─────────────────────┘-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    you get approximately:-->

<!--    ```text-->
<!--    ┌─────────────────────┐-->
<!--    │                     │-->
<!--    │    Hello Widget!    │-->
<!--    │     [Open App]      │-->
<!--    │                     │-->
<!--    └─────────────────────┘-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    Important distinction:-->

<!--    * `android:gravity` → positions the **content/children inside this view**-->
<!--    * `android:layout_gravity` → positions **this view inside its parent**-->

<!--    -&#45;&#45;-->

<!--    ### 8. Padding-->

<!--    ```xml-->
<!--    android:padding="16dp">-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    `padding` creates space **inside** the LinearLayout around its content.-->

<!--    `16dp` means 16 density-independent pixels.-->

<!--    Conceptually:-->

<!--    ```text-->
<!--    ┌─────────────────────────┐-->
<!--    │ ← 16dp →                │-->
<!--    │                         │-->
<!--    │      Hello Widget!      │-->
<!--    │                         │-->
<!--    └─────────────────────────┘-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    The `>` ends the opening `LinearLayout` tag.-->

<!--    -&#45;&#45;-->

<!--    # 9. TextView-->

<!--    ```xml-->
<!--    <TextView-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    `TextView` is an Android UI component used to **display text**.-->

<!--    In your case:-->

<!--    ```text-->
<!--    Hello Widget!-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    -&#45;&#45;-->

<!--    ### 10. TextView width-->

<!--    ```xml-->
<!--    android:layout_width="wrap_content"-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    `wrap_content` means:-->

<!--    > Make the view only as wide as its content requires.-->

<!--    For:-->

<!--    ```text-->
<!--    Hello Widget!-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    the TextView will be roughly the width required to display that text.-->

<!--    Compare:-->

<!--    ```xml-->
<!--    match_parent-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    → entire available width.-->

<!--    ```xml-->
<!--    wrap_content-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    → only what's needed.-->

<!--    -&#45;&#45;-->

<!--    ### 11. TextView height-->

<!--    ```xml-->
<!--    android:layout_height="wrap_content"-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    Same concept for height.-->

<!--    The TextView becomes only as tall as necessary to display the text.-->

<!--    -&#45;&#45;-->

<!--    ### 12. Text-->

<!--    ```xml-->
<!--    android:text="Hello Widget!"-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    This specifies what the TextView displays.-->

<!--    The result is:-->

<!--    ```text-->
<!--    Hello Widget!-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    -&#45;&#45;-->

<!--    ### 13. Text size-->

<!--    ```xml-->
<!--    android:textSize="20sp"-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    Sets the text size to `20sp`.-->

<!--    `sp` means **scale-independent pixels**.-->

<!--    `sp` is normally used for text sizes because it respects the user's font-size/accessibility settings.-->

<!--    So:-->

<!--    ```xml-->
<!--    20sp-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    means approximately a 20sp text size.-->

<!--    -&#45;&#45;-->

<!--    ### 14. Text style-->

<!--    ```xml-->
<!--    android:textStyle="bold" />-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    Makes the text bold.-->

<!--    Without it:-->

<!--    ```text-->
<!--    Hello Widget!-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    With it:-->

<!--    ```text-->
<!--    Hello Widget!-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    but rendered with a heavier/bolder font.-->

<!--    The `/ >` combination:-->

<!--    ```xml-->
<!--    />-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    means:-->

<!--    > This `TextView` has no child elements, so close it here.-->

<!--    -&#45;&#45;-->

<!--    # 15. Button-->

<!--    ```xml-->
<!--    <Button-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    Creates an Android `Button`.-->

<!--    Your widget will show:-->

<!--    ```text-->
<!--    [ Open App ]-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    -&#45;&#45;-->

<!--    ### 16. Button ID-->

<!--    ```xml-->
<!--    android:id="@+id/widget_button"-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    This gives the Button an ID:-->

<!--    ```text-->
<!--    widget_button-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    The `@+id/` part means:-->

<!--    > Create a new Android resource ID named `widget_button`.-->

<!--    Later, Android code can refer to this button using its ID.-->

<!--    For example:-->

<!--    ```kotlin-->
<!--    R.id.widget_button-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    This becomes particularly important because you want the button to perform an action when the user taps it.-->

<!--    -&#45;&#45;-->

<!--    ### 17. Button width-->

<!--    ```xml-->
<!--    android:layout_width="wrap_content"-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    The button will be only as wide as necessary for its content:-->

<!--    ```text-->
<!--    ┌──────────────┐-->
<!--    │   Open App   │-->
<!--    └──────────────┘-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    -&#45;&#45;-->

<!--    ### 18. Button height-->

<!--    ```xml-->
<!--    android:layout_height="wrap_content"-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    The button takes only the height it needs.-->

<!--    -&#45;&#45;-->

<!--    ### 19. Margin-->

<!--    ```xml-->
<!--    android:layout_marginTop="12dp"-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    Creates **12dp of space above the Button**.-->

<!--    So:-->

<!--    ```text-->
<!--    Hello Widget!-->


<!--    12dp-->


<!--    [ Open App ]-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    This is different from padding.-->

<!--    **Padding:**-->

<!--    ```text-->
<!--    View-->
<!--    ┌─────────────────┐-->
<!--    │   content       │-->
<!--    └─────────────────┘-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    Space **inside** the view.-->

<!--    **Margin:**-->

<!--    ```text-->
<!--    View A-->

<!--    ← space →-->

<!--    View B-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    Space **outside** the view.-->

<!--    -&#45;&#45;-->

<!--    ### 20. Button text-->

<!--    ```xml-->
<!--    android:text="Open App" />-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    Sets the text displayed on the button:-->

<!--    ```text-->
<!--    ┌──────────────┐-->
<!--    │   Open App   │-->
<!--    └──────────────┘-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    Again, `/>` closes the Button because it doesn't contain any child elements.-->

<!--    -&#45;&#45;-->

<!--    # 21. Closing LinearLayout-->

<!--    ```xml-->
<!--</LinearLayout>-->
<!--```-->

<!--This closes the root `LinearLayout`.-->

<!--Everything between:-->

<!--```xml-->
<!--<LinearLayout>-->
<!--    ```-->

<!--    and:-->

<!--    ```xml-->
<!--</LinearLayout>-->
<!--```-->

<!--is a **child of the LinearLayout**.-->

<!--So the hierarchy is:-->

<!--```text-->
<!--LinearLayout-->
<!--│-->
<!--├── TextView-->
<!--│   ├── Hello Widget!-->
<!--│-->
<!--└── Button-->
<!--├── Open App-->
<!--```-->

<!--And because:-->

<!--```xml-->
<!--android:orientation="vertical"-->
<!--```-->

<!--the final layout is:-->

<!--```text-->
<!--┌─────────────────────────────┐-->
<!--│                             │-->
<!--│                             │-->
<!--│       Hello Widget!         │-->
<!--│                             │-->
<!--│        ┌─────────┐          │-->
<!--│        │ Open App│          │-->
<!--│        └─────────┘          │-->
<!--│                             │-->
<!--│                             │-->
<!--└─────────────────────────────┘-->
<!--```-->

<!--### The most important concepts to understand now-->

<!--| XML            | Meaning                          |-->
<!--| &#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45; | &#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45; |-->
<!--| `LinearLayout` | Container for other views        |-->
<!--| `orientation`  | Direction of children            |-->
<!--| `vertical`     | Top → bottom                     |-->
<!--| `horizontal`   | Left → right                     |-->
<!--| `match_parent` | Take available space             |-->
<!--| `wrap_content` | Take only required space         |-->
<!--| `gravity`      | Position content inside the view |-->
<!--| `padding`      | Space inside the view            |-->
<!--| `margin`       | Space outside the view           |-->
<!--| `TextView`     | Displays text                    |-->
<!--| `Button`       | Clickable button                 |-->
<!--| `id`           | Unique identifier for a view     |-->
<!--| `dp`           | Size unit for layouts            |-->
<!--| `sp`           | Size unit for text               |-->

<!--And **one correction before you use this file**:-->

<!--```xml-->
<!--<LinerLayout-->
<!--```-->

<!--must be:-->

<!--```xml-->
<!--<LinearLayout-->
<!--```-->

<!--Otherwise Android will not recognize the root layout.-->
